msgid "Some short words ending in <0>-s</0> also end their third form in <1>-st</1>, but each changes in its own way: <2>uks, ukse, ust</2>; <3>laps, lapse, last</3>; <4>mees, mehe, meest</4>. Learn all three forms of those."
msgstr "Some short words ending in <0>-s</0> also end their third form in <1>-st</1>, but each changes in its own way: <2>uks, ukse, ust</2>; <3>laps, lapse, last</3>; <4>mees, mehe, meest</4>. Learn all three forms of those."

msgid "Some words give their third form away. Most words ending in <0>-ne</0> have a second form in <1>-se</1> and a third in <2>-st</2>: <3/>, <4/>, <5/>. Most words ending in <6>-us</6> do the same: <7/>, question, goes <8>küsimuse, küsimust</8>."
msgstr "Some words give their third form away. Most words ending in <0>-ne</0> have a second form in <1>-se</1> and a third in <2>-st</2>: <3/>, <4/>, <5/>. Most words ending in <6>-us</6> do the same: <7/>, question, goes <8>küsimuse, küsimust</8>."

