msgid "The first is the word on its own. The second is what lesson {stems} called the stem: put <0>-s</0> on it and you have <1/>. Lesson {genitive} shows what the second form means by itself, and lesson {partitive} what the third is for."
msgstr "The first is the word on its own. The second is what lesson {stems} called the stem: put <0>-s</0> on it and you have <1/>. Lesson {genitive} shows what the second form means by itself, and lesson {partitive} what the third is for."

msgid "The left column, top to bottom: the first, second and third form. Pick another word and watch how they change."
msgstr "The left column, top to bottom: the first, second and third form. Pick another word and watch how they change."

msgid "the main forms: a word’s first, second and third form"
msgstr "the main forms: a word’s first, second and third form"

msgid "The order is first, second, third, so <0>vastuse</0> comes before <1>vastust</1>."
msgstr "The order is first, second, third, so <0>vastuse</0> comes before <1>vastust</1>."

msgid "The order is first, second, third. <0>Poe</0>, the one without the <1>d</1>, comes second."
msgstr "The order is first, second, third. <0>Poe</0>, the one without the <1>d</1>, comes second."

msgid "The second and third form of {first}."
msgstr "The second and third form of {first}."

msgid "The second drops the <0>d</0> and one <1>o</1>; the third has them back."
msgstr "The second drops the <0>d</0> and one <1>o</1>; the third has them back."

msgid "The second drops the <0>d</0>; the third has it back."
msgstr "The second drops the <0>d</0>; the third has it back."

msgid "The second drops the <0>g</0>; the third has it back."
msgstr "The second drops the <0>g</0>; the third has it back."

msgid "The second form is the one <0>-s</0> and <1>-l</1> go on: <2>kooli</2> gives <3>koolis</3>."
msgstr "The second form is the one <0>-s</0> and <1>-l</1> go on: <2>kooli</2> gives <3>koolis</3>."

